{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-ns-obstruction","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:ns-obstruction","kind":"definition","title":"NS obstruction class $\\mathrm{NS}(A)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-ns-regular-qou"],"tags":["definition","obstruction","navier-stokes","euler-characteristic","categorical","spectral-gap"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstruction","text":"ns-obstruction.md","leanSource":"ns-obstruction.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:ns-obstruction\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(A, \\varTheta)</code> be a valid quantum universe over a spectral surface <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}</code> with Reeb bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>. Its <strong>NS obstruction class</strong> is the global Euler class of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code> in the surface realisation (<a href=\"#def:ns-regular-qou\" data-at=\"fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction-statement\">NS-regular QOU</a>):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{NS}(A) \\;=\\; e(\\xi) \\;\\in\\; H^2(\\mathcal{S}, \\mathbb{Z}) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.md","heading":"Definition","number":"20.5.12","page":"b/def-ns-obstruction","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.FluidDynamics.NSObstruction","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
